ITEMS = ((('what should i do for a blister at home', 'how do i treat a blister at home', 'what is the best way to handle a blister', 'how to care for a new blister', 'what helps a painful blister', 'how do you look after a blister', 'what to do when a blister appears', 'how can i treat a blister safely', 'what is the first aid for a blister', 'how should i deal with a blister on my foot'), 'For a blister, stop the rubbing that caused it, clean the area gently and leave the skin intact. Cover it with a soft dressing to protect it from friction. Ask a pharmacist or doctor if the blister is large, infected or keeps returning.'), (('should i pop a blister', 'is it ok to burst a blister', 'why should you not break a blister', 'should a blister be left intact', 'can i lance a blister at home', 'what happens if i pop a blister', 'should i drain the fluid from a blister', 'is breaking a blister a bad idea', 'what if i accidentally burst a blister', 'how to deal with a blister that has popped'), 'It is best to leave a blister intact because the roof protects the raw skin underneath from infection. If it has already burst, wash the area gently and cover it with a clean dressing. Get medical advice if the skin looks red, weeping or increasingly sore.'), (('what to do for a blister from new shoes', 'how to treat a friction blister on my heel', 'what helps a blister caused by rubbing', 'how do i care for a blister after walking', 'should i keep wearing shoes with a blister', 'what stops a shoe blister from worsening', 'how to protect a blister on the foot', 'can i pad a blister inside my shoe', 'what is best for a rubbing blister', 'how do you treat a blister on the ankle'), 'Change out of the shoes that caused the friction and wash the foot. Cover the blister with a soft pad or dressing before wearing anything over it. Seek help from a pharmacist if the area becomes hot, swollen or painful to walk on.'), (('how do i treat a blister from a burn', 'what to do with a blister after a minor burn', 'should a burn blister be popped', 'how to care for a blister caused by heat', 'can i cover a burn blister', 'what if a burn blister breaks', 'how to protect a blister after scalding', 'is a blister from a burn serious', 'what dressing helps a burn blister', 'when to get help for a burn blister'), 'A blister caused by a burn should be cooled and covered loosely without being popped. Keep it clean and avoid pressure on the area. Ask a doctor if the blister is on the face, hand or a joint, or if the surrounding skin is very red.'), (('what dressing is best for a blister', 'how do i cover a blister with a plaster', 'should i wrap a blister', 'can i use a hydrocolloid dressing on a blister', 'how to dress a blister on my hand', 'should a blister dressing be tight', 'what can i put over a blister', 'how often should a blister dressing be changed', 'is a bandage needed for a small blister', 'how to keep a blister covered at work'), 'A soft non-stick dressing or a blister plaster can cushion the area and keep it clean. Apply it without pulling the skin tight, and replace it if it becomes wet or dirty. Ask a pharmacist if you are unsure which dressing suits your blister.'), (('how do i know if a blister is infected', 'what are the signs of an infected blister', 'what if a blister has pus in it', 'can a blister get infected', 'what if the skin around a blister is red', 'how to tell if a blister is healing properly', 'what if a blister starts to smell', 'should i worry about a hot blister', 'when to check a blister for infection', 'what if a blister keeps weeping'), 'Watch for spreading redness, warmth, pus, a bad smell or fever around a blister. Keep the area covered and clean, and avoid scratching it. Ask a doctor if any of these signs appear or the blister does not settle.'), (('how to treat a blister on the sole of the foot', 'what helps a blister between the toes', 'should i cover a blister on my heel', 'how do i walk with a blister on my foot', 'what to do for a blister after a long hike', 'can i soak a blister on my foot', 'how to stop a foot blister rubbing', 'what if a blister on the foot is big', 'should i see a doctor for a foot blister', 'how long does a blister on the foot take to heal'), 'Rest the foot if you can and protect the blister with a soft dressing and clean socks. Avoid soaking it, as wet skin breaks down more easily. Ask a doctor or podiatrist if the blister is very large, infected or keeps coming back.'), (('what to do for a blister on a finger', 'how to treat a blister on the hand', 'should i cover a blister on my thumb', 'what if a blister bursts on my hand', 'how do i protect a blister at work', 'can i wear gloves over a blister', 'what helps a blister caused by tools', 'how to care for a blister on the palm', 'is a blister on the hand serious', 'when to get help for a hand blister'), 'Clean a blister on the hand and cover it with a non-stick dressing before using gloves or tools. Try to avoid gripping tightly until it heals. Seek advice from a pharmacist or doctor if it is painful, spreading or shows signs of infection.'), (('how should i cover a blister after sunburn', 'is it safe to burst a sunburn blister', 'how to cover sunburn blisters', 'what if sunburn causes a blister to burst', 'is a blister from the sun serious', 'how to care for blistered sunburnt skin', 'can i put lotion on a sunburn blister', 'what helps blisters after too much sun', 'when to get help for sunburn blisters', 'how to stop sunburn blisters rubbing'), 'Keep a sunburn blister intact and cover it loosely with a clean soft cloth to prevent rubbing. Use a gentle moisturiser around it, but avoid harsh products on the broken skin. Get medical advice if many blisters appear or you feel feverish.'), (('when should i get help for a blister', 'what if a blister is very large', 'should i go to the doctor about a blister', 'when is a blister an emergency', 'what if blisters keep coming back', 'should i worry about a blister that hurts', 'what if a blister is on my face', 'when to call a pharmacist about a blister', 'how do i know if a blister needs treatment', 'what if a blister will not heal'), 'Get medical advice for a blister that is very large, on the face, recurrent, or showing signs of infection. Seek prompt help if it follows a burn or injury and the skin looks deep. Call emergency services if the area is rapidly swelling or breathing is affected.'))
